id: pm-3e1u
title: Relocate the preset catalog out of manifest.json and guard the closed manifest vocabulary
description: "pm-cli 2026.8.19 made its extension-manifest vocabulary a closed set of 18 keys; the inert top-level pm compatibility blob and the embedded presets catalog now produce manifest_unknown_key warnings (observed as strict-assertion CI failures in unbraind/pm-linear PRs #75 and #76). Move the preset catalog to presets.json, update tests/registry.test.ts to read it from there, delete the inert pm key, pin @unbrained/pm-cli to 2026.8.22, ship presets.json in the npm package files, and add a regression test asserting checkExtensionManifestCompatibility reports zero manifest_unknown_key findings."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-22T17:50:40.903Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T17:51:22.365Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T17:51:22.256Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T17:51:22.256Z"
author: ox-alpha
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T17:50:44.022Z",ox-alpha,"Verified by temporarily re-adding the pm key: tests/manifest-vocabulary.test.ts fails while any unknown key is present and passes once removed. Relocated catalog verified byte-equivalent via registry sync test. npm test: 74 pass 0 fail. release:check exit 0. ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit exit 0 on pinned 2026.8.22."
files[6]{path,scope}:
